-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",2,{
[33]="70072BF2\n1\tExamine the line of Orc-made barricades in the woods between Imhûlar and Adagím\tA line of Orc-made barricades runs from north to south in the woods between Imhûlar and Adagím.\n2\tFind the entrance to Mauthark, south-east of the barricades you discovered\tThe Orc camp of Mauthark lies to the south-east of the line of barricades you discovered.\n3\tCollect deadly knives from Orcs at Mauthark (total: 8)\tThe Orcs of Mauthark carry deadly knives with which they threaten the Kintai who live in Adagím.\n4\tLeave the Orc-knives in a strongbox at Laivárth, the Kinta grove to the north-east\tThe nearest grove of the Kintai should be Laivárth, located far to the north-east of Mauthark. The Elves there will have a strongbox in which you can deposit the deadly Orc-knives.\n5\tCompleted\tThe Kintai who tend the grove of Laivárth will be appreciative of your efforts against the Orcs dwelling at Mauthark.\n",
[34]="700718E7\n1\tPlace torches near the crypt entrances (total: 9)\tGíshgi is uncomfortable with the nearby wights. She has a theory that they may fear flames enough that placing lit torches at the entrances to the crypts would keep the wights within, and has asked you to try it. There are crypt entrances at Gadim-ûn, Naxar Dâl, and the Crypts of Khâb Daku in north-eastern An Shêru.\n2\tTalk to Gíshgi in Gadim-ûn\tYou have placed lit torches at the entrances of the crypts in north-eastern An Shêru in an effort to ward off the wights and keep them inside, where they belong. You should return to Gíshgi in Gadim-ûn and tell her of your success.\n",
[35]="70040EC3\n1\tCollect waterlogged barrels in the Bay of Belfalas (total: 6)\030Collect waterlogged crates in the Bay of Belfalas (total: 4)\tWaterlogged crates and barrels can be found on the shores of the Bay of Belfalas and in and around Edhellond. You have discovered numerous supplies that have survived their journey down the Blackroot and Ringló. You should recover them for the people of Gondor.\n2\tDeliver the waterlogged barrels and crates to Dolvir\tDolvir can be found on a hilltop to the east of Edhellond. You have gathered many waterlogged crates and barrels in the Bay of Belfalas and should now return them to Dolvir.\n",
[36]="7003A4CD\n1\tTravel to Beaconwatch\tBeaconwatch is south along the road. Meregyth told you to meet her at Beaconwatch.\n2\tTalk to Meregyth\tMeregyth might be found near the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. You have found safety within the fortified walls of Beaconwatch and should now seek out Meregyth to ensure that she arrived safely.\n",
[37]="7002C006\n1\tBring the broken weapon to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is in the Last Homely House in Rivendell, far from the Great River. You should bring the broken weapon to Elrond and see if his smiths can reforge it.\n",
[38]="70058CEF\n1\tPick up the bucket of water by the Greylin\tA bucket of water can be found along the Greylin near Khadâsh-gâra. Nagli Want-kin has asked you to aid him in bathing his beloved aurochs, Lapis. You should fetch a bucket of water as he asked and use it to bathe Lapis.\n2\tTalk to Nagli Want-kin\tNagli Want-kin can be found at Khadâsh-gâra in Elderslade. You have bathed Lapis and she seems to be very happy about it. You should talk to Nagli.\n",
[39]="70017529\n1\tDefeat grodbog-warriors (total: 10)\030Defeat grodbog hive-defenders (total: 6)\030Defeat blind drones (total: 4)\tSkûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Lar wants to see the gredbyg within the depths of Skûmfil defeated. The insects are trying to breed in the bodies dumped by the Orcs within Skûmfil, and if left unchecked, they could breed too quickly to control. Lar also wonders if they might be the source of the plague affecting the Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Lar at the Shadowed Refuge\tLar is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil. You fought against numerous and varied gredbyg within Skûmfil and now must return to the Shadowed Refuge to inform Lar of your success.\n",
[40]="7005296B\n1\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n2\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[41]="7002CA91\n1\tHarvest the crops from the seeds you planted (total: 5)\030Collect eggs (total: 5)\030Pull weeds (total: 5)\tTatwine, happy with his new position as a free man maintaining the farming work you started, has invited you to join him in his maintenance of the farm. You should help Tatwine with the farm chores.\n2\tReturn to Tatwine\tTatwine is tending the fields at the abandoned farm. You should return to Tatwine with the goods you gathered.\n",
[42]="70002DF2\n1\tTalk to Arifael\tArifael lives on the slope of Amon Nendir, south of the High Moor on the eastern edge of the Trollshaws. Arifael has asked for your aid against his distant kinsmen from the mountains.\n2\tTalk to Arifael\tArifael lives on the slope of Amon Nendir, east of the High Moor on the eastern edge of the Trollshaws. You have aided in warding off Arifael's distant kinsmen from the Misty Mountains. You should speak to him.\n",
[43]="700683D2\n1\tCollect dirt-encrusted baubles from sea-hawk nests ([see journal]/14)\tLuthana requested that you search for sea-hawk nests far to the north for baubles and trinkets stolen from shipwrecks. She will use the baubles to satisfy her patrons in Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver the baubles to Luthana at the hunter's expedition\tYou collected enough baubles to satisfy Luthana's patrons in Umbar Baharbêl. Deliver the baubles to her at the expedition camp in the south-eastern area of the Cape of Umbar.\n",
[44]="70001812\n1\tDefeat north-hawks (total: 6)\tThere are North-hawks all throughout the hills around Othrikar. Hlája Sagasong has asked you to assist the Dwarves of Othrikar by slaying as many hendrevail as you can.\n2\tReturn to Hlája Sagasong\tHlája Sagasong is at Othrikar. Hlája Sagasong sent you to slay the hendrevail flocking in the hills around Othrikar. You should return to him with the news of your success.\n",
[45]="70028188\n1\tDefeat Dievlig Dunlendings (total: 8)\tEvil Dunlendings may be found along the path and up the hill south of Bledhun. Bledhun asked you to seek out and defeat the Dievlig that hold the hill.\n2\tTalk to Bledhun in the Bonevales\tBledhun awaits you in the north, down the hill. You should return to Bledhun and let him know that you have driven back the Dievlig on the hill.\n",
[46]="7000E8FB\n1\tCollect Blagrove's Brown from the Bird and Baby\tBlagrove's Brown can be purchased at The Bird and Baby Inn, in Michel Delving. You should buy some Blagrove's Brown for delivery to Harigar Mudbottom, who waits in Oatbarton.\n2\tBring the Blagrove's Brown to Harigar Mudbottom\tThe Bird and Baby Inn is in Michel Delving. Harigar Mudbottom is in Oatbarton. Harigar Mudbottom told you of the horror he experienced when he realized he had never had a \"Blagrove's Brown\" from the Bird and Baby. Since he lied and told others that he had, he has asked you, in the strictest of confidence, to fetch him a mug of the ale so that he can truly say he has had a sip of every ale, wine, and spirit that can be found west of the Misty Mountains.\n",
[47]="70025966\n1\tCollect essences (total: 8)\tEssences can be found on the limrafn among the Barandalf, north of Dwaling. Pearl Goodbody has asked you to gather essences from the limrafn within the dunes.\n2\tBring the essences to Pearl Goodbody in Dwaling\tPearl Goodbody is at Hob Hillbrow's just outside of Dwaling. Pearl Goodbody will be eager to see the limrafn essences you have gathered for her.\n",
[48]="700216DB\n1\tCollect fake Blagrove's Brown from The Ivy Bush in Hobbiton\tThe Ivy Bush is in Hobbiton in the Shire. You should speak with the tavern keep at The Ivy Bush and collect some Whitebranch. This will be used as a decoy Blagrove's Brown.\n2\tBring the fake Blagrove's Brown to Harigar Mudbottom in Oatbarton\tHarigar Mudbottom is in Oatbarton, the northern-most town in the Shire. You should bring the fake Blagrove's Brown, secretly Whitebranch, to Harigar Mudbottom.\n",
[49]="7006B87B\n1\tCollect crunchy vegetables (total: 6)\tAkûshu has asked you to find crunchy vegetables for the horses to snack on to relieve their distress. Crunchy vegetables can be found along the river-bank just south of Eshadûr.\n2\tYou have collected crunchy vegetables for the horses at the stranded caravan to snack upon. You should give one to each horse.\t\n3\tTalk to Akûshu\tYou have given each horse at the stranded caravan a crunchy vegetable to snack upon. You should talk to Akûshu.\n",
[50]="7002D3CB\n1\tDefeat goblins in the Hall of the High Stair (total: 10)\tThe Hall of the High Stair can be found to the north of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Rink has asked you to defeat any goblin inhabitants in the Hall of the High Stair.\n2\tTalk to Rink at the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tRink is at the Chamber of the Cross-roads, south of The Hall of the High Stair. You have managed to overcome several of the goblins in combat, and Rink awaits word of your deed.\n",
[51]="70035706\n1\tSpeak with Oswi in Scylfig\tCyneberg, stricken by grief from the loss of her father and Thrymm, has asked you to leave her alone. You should help the survivors in Scylfig break the strange ice left in the wake of the attack.\n2\tClear the ice shards from Oswi's home\tIce shards can be found in front of the door to Oswi's home. You should clear the shards from Oswi's home.\n3\tSpeak with Portred\tCyneberg, stricken by grief from the loss of her father and Thrymm, has asked you to leave her alone. You should help the survivors in Scylfig break the strange ice left in the wake of the attack.\n4\tClear ice shards from the stable\tIce shards can be found in front of the stable near Portred. You should clear the shards to free Portred's horse.\n5\tSpeak with Saxburg\tCyneberg, stricken by grief from the loss of her father and Thrymm, has asked you to leave her alone. You should help the survivors in Scylfig break the strange ice left in the wake of the attack.\n6\tRemove ice shards from in front of the barn door\tIce shards can be found blocking the door to the barn near Saxburg. You should clear away the shards of ice.\n7\tTry to speak with Cyneberg again\tCyneberg is in Scylfig. You have aided the villagers, and should now see if Cyneberg is recovered enough to speak with you.\n",
[52]="7002BFDC\n1\tDefeat Khundolar in the Brown Lands (total: 6)\tKhundolar Easterlings can be found throughout the Brown Lands, but especially at their encampment, Lashkarg, to the south of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Dagbert has asked you to defeat a few Khundolar Easterlings to prove to Céola that they can and must be dealt with immediately.\n2\tTalk to Dagbert at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tDagbert is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north of Lashkarg. You should return to Dagbert with news of your success.\n",
[53]="7002EA46\n1\tDefeat Khundolar in the Brown Lands (total: 6)\tKhundolar Easterlings can be found throughout the Brown Lands, but especially at their encampment, Lashkarg, to the south of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Céola has asked you to defeat a few Khundolar Easterlings to get an estimate of their strength.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north of Lashkarg. You should return to Céola with news of your success.\n",
[54]="7006672A\n1\tCollect silkencaps in Lhingroth (total: 10)\tSilkencaps, a pale mushroom native to the Blackroot Vale, can be found in the caverns of Lhingroth in the hills to the south-east of Sardol. Sidharan has asked you to collect silkencaps from the caverns of Lhingroth, but he has warned you that spiders dwell in Lhingroth. You should collect the silkencaps and deliver them to Sidharan in Sardol.\n2\tDeliver the silkencaps to Sidharan in Sardol\tSidharan can be found in Sardol. You have collected many silkencaps from the caverns of Lhingroth. You should deliver them to Sidharan in Sardol.\n",
[55]="700076AA\n1\tTalk to Lofar Ironband\tLofar can be found at the stone cottage north of the Bree cross-roads. Kenton Thistleway told you that Blake, the brigand-captain, will kill his daughter unless he gets a new sword. Kenton has asked you to retrieve the sword from Lofar.\n2\tFind Maribell Thistleway\tBlake's brigand camp is in the Bree-fields, north-west of Bree-town, directly west of Grimbriar's Post. When you spoke with Lofar, he told you that the sword was not ready yet. He urged you to go to Blake's brigand camp and try to convince the brigand-captain not to harm Kenton's daughter. The sword will be ready soon. He also suggested you take friends in case there was trouble.\n3\tTalk to Kenton Thistleway at Thornley's Work-site\tKenton Thistleway can be found at the southern most section of Thornley's Work-site, north along the Greenway. Blake, the brigand-captain, took Kenton Thistleway's daughter, Maribell, captive. You rescued Maribell, who has returned to Bree. You should return to Kenton with news of your success.\n",
[56]="7006EB86\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside Kûr Anzar to begin the assault\tMeet with Mizâdi outside the gates of Kûr Anzar to begin the assault.\n2\tDefeat All-seeing in Kûr Anzar (total: 16)\030Restore Mizâdi's standard throughout Kûr Anzar (total: 8)\tMake your way through Kûr Anzar, tearing down Barkhûshim banners and replacing them with banners for Renewed Hamât. Defeat All-seeing cultists throughout Kûr Anzar.\n3\tMake your way to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar\tMake your way to Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.\n4\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the tower of Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the tower of Kûr Anzar.\n",
[57]="7006EB8F\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready.\n2\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tower in Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tower in Kûr Anzar.\n",
[58]="7006EB83\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi about her plan to save Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tower in order to help Kûr Anzar from going up in flame!\n2\tSpeak with Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi near the tower of Kûr Anzar.\n",
[59]="7000006C\n1\tTalk to Ultan Foebane\tUltan Foebane is at the Combe-gate on the east side of the town of Bree. You have been told to speak with Ultan Foebane, a mighty champion travelling through the Bree-land, for the dwarf may be able to help you become stronger.\n2\tDefeat Zhurpukh of the Deeps\030Defeat Fair Sherman\030Defeat Morley the Fierce\tUltan Foebane has given you a list containing the locations of three deadly enemies to dispatch. To prove you are a worthy champion, Ultan Foebane has tasked you with slaying three threats to the folk of Bree-land.\n3\tTalk to Ultan Foebane\tUltan Foebane is at the Combe-gate on the east side of the town of Bree. You have defeated the three opponents that Ultan Foebane challenged you to best and should now return in victory to the dwarf.\n",
[60]="7006BF0A\n1\tCull diseased boars in Shakhdag (total: 9)\030Cull diseased servals and caracals in Tir Katar (total: 7)\tSurodith asks you to cull afflicted boars and servals plagued by the Lâg Dávrit in Shakhdag and Tir Katar. Shakhdag is north-west of Vartúlin. Tir Katar is directly north of Vartúlin.\n2\tSpeak with Surodith in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Surodith in Vartúlin and report your success.\n",
[61]="7000AC4A\n1\tDeliver the materials to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Grimwood-kindling (total: 3)\030Collect Grimwood Log (total: 2)\030Collect Grimwood Root (total: 3)\030Collect Grimwood Heartwood\tHead south from Tol Ascarnen into Hithlad to seek out the wood needed to build the signal fires to the south. Though your forces took Tol Ascarnen, the keep is woefully undefended, and Kaasak has ordered you to build a pyre to call in reinforcements from the south. You should make your way into the Ettenmoors and search for kindling, timber, and larger logs to build a beacon fire large enough to call in reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[62]="7000AC4C\n1\tDeliver the materials to Soldier Kaasak at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Grimwood-kindling (total: 3)\030Collect Grimwood Log (total: 2)\030Collect Grimwood Root (total: 3)\030Collect Grimwood Heartwood\tHead south of Tol Ascarnen into Hithlad and the Grimwood forest to collect the wood needed to build the blaze. Though your forces took Tol Ascarnen, the keep is woefully undefended, and Kaasak has ordered you to build a pyre to call in reinforcements from the west. You should make your way into the Ettenmoors and search for kindling, timber, and larger logs to build a beacon fire large enough to call in reinforcements to Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[63]="7000AC4B\n1\tStand in the open among the trees near Tol Ascarnen's western wall\tMake your way to the copse of trees in the woods on the western side of Tol Ascarnen. Make your presence know there. Paashum asked you to make your way into the small section of woods on the western shore of Hoardale near Tol Ascarnen. He hopes to send a force into the keep after setting the woods ablaze. You will need to be obvious enough to attract the enemy's attention.\n",
[64]="7002C8FF\n1\tEnter into the Orc-cave\tThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan. Frithstan believes that his men have been taken alive and are being held within the nearby Orc-caves.\n2\tTalk to the first captive and release him\tThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan. The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.\n3\tTalk to the second captive and release him\tThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan. The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.\n4\tRescue the third captive from his cell\tThe entrance to the Orc-caves may be found along the western rock wall in the Wailing Hills, behind the Orc-camp that held Frithstan. The Rohirrim-captives are being held within caves by the Mor-hai Orcs.\n5\tReturn to Frithstan's camp and talk to Frithstan\tFrithstan can be found at his camp to along the road north of the Cuthstan. He awaits your return from the Orc-caves.\n",
})
